6:T4b7,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","headline":"BaZi Symbolic Stars: Peach Blossom, Academic Star & Shen Sha Explained","description":"Understand BaZi Shen Sha symbolic stars — Peach Blossom, Academic Star, the Year Pillar, and the \"life star\" concept.","image":"https://fourpillarscalculator.com/og-image.jpg","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Imperial BaZi","legalName":"Gesmine-Invest Limited","identifier":{"@type":"PropertyValue","propertyID":"UK Company Number","value":"14120136"},"address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"Hardy House, 269 Poynders Gardens","addressLocality":"London","postalCode":"SW4 8PQ","addressCountry":"GB"}},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Imperial BaZi","legalName":"Gesmine-Invest Limited","identifier":{"@type":"PropertyValue","propertyID":"UK Company Number","value":"14120136"},"address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"Hardy House, 269 Poynders Gardens","addressLocality":"London","postalCode":"SW4 8PQ","addressCountry":"GB"},"logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://fourpillarscalculator.com/logo.png"}},"mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://fourpillarscalculator.com/bazi/symbolic-stars/"}}7:T8b3,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the Peach Blossom Star (桃花) in BaZi?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The Peach Blossom Star (桃花, Tao Hua) — sometimes translated as the Flower of Romance — is the classic BaZi symbolic star for charm, attraction, and romantic or social magnetism. It is derived from the Day or Year Branch and appears in a specific fixed pattern across the twelve branches. Peach Blossom is looked up from the Day Branch or Year Branch against a fixed table of four branch groups (each group of three branches shares one Peach Blossom branch). A qualified BaZi reading cross-references this against the rest of the chart before drawing conclusions — a single symbolic star is never read in isolation."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the Academic Star (文昌) in BaZi?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The Academic Star (文昌, Wen Chang) is the symbolic star most associated with intelligence, exam success, and scholarly achievement. Like Peach Blossom, it is derived from a fixed relationship to the Day Stem. Wen Chang is looked up from the Day Stem against a fixed stem-to-branch table. As with all Shen Sha, its presence adds a thematic layer — it does not override the core Day Master and Ten Gods analysis that forms the backbone of a BaZi reading."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the Year Pillar in a BaZi chart?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The Year Pillar (年柱) is the first of the Four Pillars, built from your birth year's Heavenly Stem and Earthly Branch. It traditionally represents ancestry, family background, early childhood (roughly birth to age 15), and your public-facing social image. It also carries your Chinese zodiac animal sign."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What does \"life star\" mean in BaZi?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"\"Life star\" is an informal term some readers use for the Day Master (the Day Stem) — the core element that anchors the entire chart and is treated as \"you\" in a BaZi reading. It is not a separate Shen Sha; see our Day Master guide for the full breakdown of all ten possible Day Master types."}}]}0:{"P":null,"b":"IbUSb_WijHZXdE_l5nHrj","p":"","c":["","bazi","symbolic-stars"],"i":false,"f":[[["",{"children":["bazi",{"children":["symbolic-stars",{"children":["__PAGE__",{}]}]}]},"$undefined","$undefined",true],["",["$","$1","c",{"children":[[["$","link","0",{"rel":"stylesheet","href":"/_next/static/css/97fbd51b9f13d89c.css","precedence":"next","crossOrigin":"$undefined","nonce":"$undefined"}]],["$","html",null,{"lang":"en","className":"dark scroll-smooth","children":["$","body",null,{"className":"bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 font-sans antialiased selection:bg-amber-500/30 s